  "description": "Dynamic programming primer for coding interviews: the state-transition-base-order recipe, recursion to memo to table to O(1) space, 1D DP (climbing stairs, house robber, decode ways), grid DP and a map of the DP families with recognition cues.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Coding</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Dynamic programming</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Dynamic Programming Primer: From Recursion to a Table</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Dynamic programming (DP) is \"solve each small question once, write the answer down, and build the big answer from the small ones\". This page turns that sentence into a four-step recipe you can apply under interview pressure, walks it from plain recursion to memo to table to two variables on the classic 1D and grid problems, and ends with a map of the DP families and the clue that gives each one away.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-dp-state-design\">DP state design: how to find the recurrence</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-knapsack\">Knapsack family</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-lis-lcs\">LIS and two-string DP (LCS, edit distance)</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-palindrome-interval-dp\">Palindrome DP and interval DP</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-dp-stocks-trees-games\">State-machine, tree and game DP</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-bitmask-dp\">Bitmask DP</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
